<p>
<strong>Note: This document is to be included with all tender or quotation requests and purchase orders issued.</strong>
</p>
<p>All light fixtures and lamps supplied are to be of the exact brand and model specified. The contractor is to ensure that all light fixtures and lamps will comply with all local electrical, health, and other codes.</p>

<p>The supplier should feel free to offer for approval equivalent substitute light fixtures and lamps where appropriate. Equivalent substitutes will only be acceptable on the specific written approval of the lighting designer. Approval to supply a substitute for one fixture type does not imply approval to supply a substitute for another.</p>

<p>All light fixtures and electrical accessories will be supplied on the understanding that on the request of the electrical contractor, lighting designer, or electrical engineer the luminaire or accessory supplier will furnish appropriate "approval" certificate or number (in the case of a prescribed item) or "certificates of suitability" (in the case of non prescribed item) for the luminaires or accessories supplied.</p>
<p>All MR16 and MR11 dichroic low volt lamps will be Osram brand “Decostar Energy Saver”.</p>
<p>All low volt luminaires will be supplied with suitably rated lampholders of one of the following brands: GE; Buhle; Leecraft; Vossloh Schwabe, or the luminaire supplier is to unconditionally guarantee the lampholder for 10,000 operating hours being approximately equal to 3 lamp changes.
Low voltage transformers are to be enclosed type or are to have enclosed or protected primary and secondary terminals in compliance with appropriate local codes and will be rated at the wattage of the specified connected load, except in the circumstance of single 20 watt lamps where a 20 to 25 VA transformer will be preferable but a 50 VA transformer will be acceptable. Unless otherwise specified or specific approval is sought and received from the lighting designer or electrical engineer, one transformer will be supplied and installed for each luminaire.</p>
<p>Low volt transformers are to be Osram “Halotronic Mouse” and electronic (dimmable) ballasts will be Osram “Quicktronic” series brand or equivalent only with the specific approval of the lighting designer or electrical engineer.</p>
<p>Fluorescent lamps are to be of the brand specified, of the exact colour and quality specified, or the equivalent only with the specific approval of the lighting designer. Unless otherwise specified all GLS (General Lighting Service) lamps will be frosted (pearl) types with E27 Edison screw base.</p>
<p>LED lamps are to be the exact make and model specified. Substitute LED products from other manufacturers may be offered for written approval by the lighting designer, if they meet as a minimum the following criteria:</p>
<ul>
	<li>Demonstrate colour constancy over the entire life of the LED</li>
	<li>Binning range with a maximum of +/-100K - Availability of a warm white colour temperature option (2600K-2800K)</li>
	<li>Colour rendering of > 80 - Demonstrate a proven track record of successful long term installations</li>
	<li>Availability of suitably sized heatsinks for direct application, without the need for third party additional heatsinking</li>
	<li>Must be dimmable via either direct PWM (approved by the project’s dimmer system supplier) or via control gear approved by the Lighting Designer or Electrical Engineer</li>
	<li>Linear strips must have both a low wattage (approx. 400 lumens per meter) and high wattage (approximately 800 lumens per meter) options.</li>
	<li>Availability of appropriately IP-rated housings</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Explanation of Fixture Specification Document Code.</strong> This is the code to describe the whole
fixture. fixture:</p>
<p>
	A = Allowance <br>
	B = Battery lamp<br>
	C = Candle<br>
	F = Floor lamp fixture<br>
	H = Hanging lamp fixture <br>
	I = Inground uplight <br>
	L = Linear LED fixture<br>
	M = Misc<br>
	P = Pole top or bollard<br>
	R = Recessed fixture <br>
	S = Surface mounted fixture <br>
	T = Table lamp<br>
	W = Underwater fixture<br>
	<br>
	<strong>F. Qty:</strong> This is the total number of fixtures on the project.<br><br>

	<strong>Fixture/Lamp/Accessory:</strong> This is the name of the individual components required to make up a fixture. Generally it will be either a light fitting, a lamp, or an accessory. C. Qty: This is the total number of component in the fixture.<br><br>
	
	<strong>C. Qty:</strong> This is the total number of component in the fixture.<br><br>
	
	<strong>W:</strong> This is individual lamp wattage per component.<br><br>
	
	<strong>Manufacturer:</strong> This is the manufacturer of the component. If “Generic” appears in this column, then any reputable manufacturer’s product that matches that particular component’s description may be used.<br><br>
	
	<strong>Catalogue#</strong> This is the catalogue number of the particular component.<br><br>
	
	<strong>Finish</strong> This further describes the component. This additional information typically relates to the outward appearance of the component, i.e. its colour.<br><br>
	
	<strong>Dimensions</strong> This column indicates the critical measurements of the component.<br><br>
	
	<strong>Notes</strong> This column gives further information about the component, or where to find that information.<br><br>
	
	<strong>Fixture Specification Abbreviations</strong><br><br>
	
	A = Amperes<br><br>
	CO = Cut-out diameter<br><br>
	D = Depth<br><br>
	dia = Diameter<br><br>
	ELV = Extra Low Voltage<br><br>
	GLS = General Lighting Service<br><br>
	H = Height<br><br>
	ID = Internal Diameter or Interior Designer L = Length<br><br>
	LV = Low Voltage<br><br>
	OAE = Or Approved Equivalent<br><br>
	OD = Outside Diameter<br><br>
	OL = Overall Length<br><br>
	RD = Recessed Depth<br><br>
	TBA = To Be Advised<br><br>
	TBC = To Be Confirmed<br><br>
	V = Volts or Voltage<br><br>
	VA = Volt Amperes<br><br>
	W = Watts or Wattage or Width<br><br>
	
</p>
